NUM-05: evaluate the WEIR divider equation in CFS/CMS, not in the flow units

divider_validate() and divider_getOutflow() divided Cd*Ht^1.5 by UCF(FLOW),
so the coefficient meant cfs per ft^1.5 only for CFS and cms per m^1.5 only
for CMS; the same divider diverted 5% of the flow in GPM, 76% in MGD, 3% in
LPS and 11% in MLD instead of 95%, or was rejected with ERROR 137. Convert
Cd*Ht^1.5 from CFS or CMS to internal cfs as weir_getFlow() does for weir
links (divide by M3perFT3 under SI). CFS models are unchanged; CMS models
change by the ratio of the two CMS factors (0.02832/0.028317, +0.011%).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-05_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/node.c b/src/legacy/engine/node.c
index 070db5a..829dca2 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/node.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/node.c
@@ -1223,9 +1223,9 @@ void  divider_validate(int j)
             report_writeErrorMsg(ERR_WEIR_DIVIDER, Node[j].ID);
         else
         {
-            // --- find flow when weir is full
+            // --- find flow when weir is full (Cd*Ht^1.5 is in CFS or CMS)
             Divider[k].qMax = Divider[k].cWeir * pow(Divider[k].dhMax, 1.5)
-                              / UCF(FLOW);
+                              / (UnitSystem == SI ? M3perFT3 : 1.0);
             if ( Divider[k].qMin > Divider[k].qMax )
                 report_writeErrorMsg(ERR_WEIR_DIVIDER, Node[j].ID);
         }
@@ -1285,7 +1285,8 @@ double divider_getOutflow(int j, int k)
             
             // --- otherwise use weir eqn.
             else qOut = Divider[i].cWeir *
-                        pow(f*Divider[i].dhMax, 1.5) / UCF(FLOW);
+                        pow(f*Divider[i].dhMax, 1.5) /
+                        (UnitSystem == SI ? M3perFT3 : 1.0);
         }
         break;
 
